
# A. gateway.register: Honeybee stores the endpoint and writes gateways/apiary.json itself; spawned bees are seeded with the URL

## A1 deployInfo: the two capability tags, no gateway, no skill tree
```json
{
  "capabilities": [
    "gateway.register.v1",
    "skills.install.v1"
  ],
  "gateways": [],
  "skills": null,
  "nodeId": "6eb9ee74-9e69-45e1-81c1-9a0ef3627492"
}
```

## A2 only the registered local Apiary authority on a direct Unix socket may call the verbs
```json
{
  "unregistered local caller": "caller_not_trusted (registration_required)",
  "relay lane": "caller_not_trusted",
  "unregistered skills.install": "caller_not_trusted (registration_required)"
}
```

