# B. skills.install: a content-hashed tree lands in every Honeybee-owned home now and in every home activated later

## B1 a tree that does not hash to what it claims is refused typed, before anything is written
```json
{
  "digest off by one": "invalid_request (digest)",
  "one file's sha256 lies": "invalid_request (sha256 #0)",
  "size disagrees with content": "invalid_request (size #1)",
  "path escapes with ..": "invalid_request (path #2)",
  "absolute path": "invalid_request (path #2)",
  "reserved .hive- name": "invalid_request (path #2)",
  "content not base64": "invalid_request (content #3)",
  "nodeCopyExists": false,
  "skills": null
}
```

